BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.facebook.com/events/1460568452447695/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Author Talk with Dr. Gordon Walker!
DTSTART;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260303T180000
DTEND;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260303T180000
UID:2602184aYatkfgFEKXgFniF3m09w
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special event with Gordon Walker\, author of Dr.
  Fun Guy's Passport to Kingdom Fungi: A Scientist's Guide to the Wild and 
 Wonderful World of Mushrooms\, Molds\, and More. This event is free\, but 
 we appreciate your RSVP below so we can plan for your attendance. ABOUT BU
 NNY AND CLYDE ON THE LAM Learn the basics of fungal biology\, foraging\, a
 nd identification in this in-depth illustrated introduction from the belov
 ed scientist\, mushroom enthusiast\, and social media star behind Fascinat
 ed By Fungi. In Dr. Fun Guy’s Passport to Kingdom Fungi\, Dr. Gordon Wal
 ker brings his scientific knowledge and love for everything fungi to the p
 age. The first section of this book is written in a comprehensive question
 -and-answer format. Starting with “What are fungi?\,” you’ll learn a
 bout everything from what mycelium is and fungi’s evolution and biochemi
 stry to how they are classified and how they impact our world today. You w
 ill also find information on best foraging practices and culinary techniqu
 es. The second half of this book introduces you to mushroom identification
  skills and profiles various mushrooms and other fungi\, from incredible e
 dibles you can find in the wild to the dangerously toxic\, medicinal\, and
  just plain weird. Finally\, you’ll find fungal phenomena\, showing the 
 amazing breadth and diversity of the fungal kingdom. With colorful and com
 prehensive science illustrations\, mushroom photography\, and QR codes lin
 king to resources to help you continue your fungal explorations\, this is 
 the perfect portal to step through into the world of mushrooms. “Gordon 
 Walker’s book is fun\, yes\, and richly illustrated\, but at the same ti
 me it’s an impressively detailed survey of the fungal kingdom and its fa
 scinating denizens\, mushrooms and molds\, yeasts\, and more.”—Harold 
 McGee\, author of On Food and Cooking and Nose Dive “Gordon Walker’s e
 nthusiasm on the pages \\(and in person\\) is contagious\, and he’s a gr
 eat evangelizer for popular mycology.”—Britt A. Bunyard\, PhD\, publis
 her of Fungi Magazine and author of Lives of the Fungi ABOUT THE AUTHOR Dr
 . Gordon Walker is an award-winning speaker\, science communicator\, publi
 shed author\, and social media star \\(@fascinatedbyfungi \\) with over 3 
 million cumulative followers.  He has a PhD in Biochemistry and Molecular 
 Biology from UC Davis where his research focused on the microbial ecology 
 of wine fermentations\, bioprocess control\, and yeast genetics. He is a p
 assionate advocate for mushrooms\, fungal conservation\, and environmental
  sustainability.  His new book "Passport to Kingdom Fungi" will fundamenta
 lly transform the way people learn about mushrooms and fungi\, serving as 
 the go to resource for a whole new generation of mycophiles and people int
 erested in foraging\, wild foods\, and fermentation.
LOCATION:Napa County Library
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1460568452447695/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
