SUMMARY:March Month of Flowers Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260304T000000
DTEND;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260304T120000
UID:260219vZ3uRHsgn0SD_oG4vln6nA
DESCRIPTION:**Starting March 1st begins the "March Month of Flowers Challe
 nge" (online).** \n\nYou'll receive a list of prompts for every day in Mar
 ch. \n\nCreate an art piece related to the prompt.\n\nShare in our privat
 e Facebook group.\n\nBe inspired and give inspiration to others.\n\n**Only
  $5**\, so everyone can join and share in this creative adventure!\n\n***M
 arch Month of Flowers* Challenge** is here to give you a creative outlet
 \, some structure\, and respite from your brain. \n\nWhen you pick up a b
 rush\, pen\, or pencil (thread\, clay\, fabric…)\, your brain gets a res
 t and becomes more alive and flexible. The world around you becomes more 
 alive\; you pick up on shades\, details\, and patterns all around you. Y
 our intuition gets stronger. And fear lessens\, anxiety fades\, and curios
 ity grows. You stop worrying about making mistakes\, and instead\, you fi
 nd the freedom to simply create
URL:https://www.taradickinson.com/project-page/workshops
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/intro-to-observational-drawing"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Intro to Observational Drawing — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\
 , California
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260304T000000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260305T000000
UID:56bc8dbc724036341eb7c650606ead8e@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Out of Stock\n      \n    \n\n\n\n\nIntro to Observational Dra
 wing\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $65.00\n        \n      \n  
   \n  \n\nWednesday\, March 4\, 2026\; 6-9PM$55 + $10 Materials FeeAges 16
 +In this one day introductory workshop\, participants will get a peek into
  the process of building one’s drawing abilities through developing clos
 e observational skills and learning fundamental drawing techniques. If you
  find this intro helpful and want to keep exploring\, you can sign up for 
 the 3 week class one month later.This course is for anyone who wants to pr
 actice and advance their drawing skills - beginners\, those who haven’t 
 practiced in years\, or any artists who just want to learn more and practi
 ce with consistent feedback and guidance. Learning to draw is truly learni
 ng to see - a skill that anyone can be taught\, practice\, and hone. Throu
 gh demonstration\, practice\, and reflective discussion\, this class will 
 explore the foundations of classical drawing techniques in a low pressure 
 environment. Observational drawing gives all artists a foundation of pract
 ical knowledge and skills that infinitely expands the possibilities of wha
 t one can create. If your ideas feel limited by your drawing skills\, if y
 ou feel frustrated or stuck in your painting practice\, or if you simply w
 ant to start drawing and are looking for a way to begin\, this is the clas
 s for you. About the Instructor: Hannah Day received her BA in Visual Arts
  with an emphasis on drawing and printmaking from University of San Diego\
 , then attended University of Hawaii at Manoa to receive her MFA in printm
 aking. Hannah’s etchings have been internationally shown and collected\,
  but her personal practice also includes paper cutting\, graphite\, waterc
 olor\, mixed media\, and murals. She have taught all ages and many formats
  (kids\, teens\, adults\, college\, private lessons\, camps\, etc) and man
 y mediums. These days Hannah has been teaching primarily paper cutting but
  also enjoys teaching drawing\, painting and printmaking.\n\n\n\n\n\n     
    \n          \n            \n              Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/intro-to-observational-drawin
 g
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
