X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.skyranchgallery.com", "Press Democrat": "https://www.skyranchgallery.com"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.skyranchgallery.com"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Sky Ranch Gallery presents Mary McDougall as the March Featured Ar
 tist
DTSTART;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260305T110000
DTEND;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260305T140000
UID:260228K0eIN-5RtEWW6UvcbjJG3Q
DESCRIPTION:Homeward Bound 12x12 acrylic\n\nMary McDougall is a retired po
 tter turned painter. As a painter her first love is landscapes\, as she sa
 ys\, “It is all about Mother Earth”. Living in the midst of such beaut
 y\, her paintings often depict the quiet serenity and explosive color of t
 he trees\, rolling hills\, vineyards\, wildflowers and coastal views. Mary
  is a member of Sky Ranch Gallery in Tomales and is the Featured Artist fo
 r the month of March with her acrylics and watercolors.
LOCATION:Sky Ranch Gallery
URL:https://www.skyranchgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/an-abstract-vision/", "Press Democrat": "https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/an-abstract-vision/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/an-abstract-vision/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:An Abstract Vision
DTSTART;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260305T110000
DTEND;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260305T180000
UID:260227mQrlz9TaxEOrHvsPoI5nZQ
DESCRIPTION:**Exhibition runs April 4 - May 30\, 2026**\n\nDeadline for En
 tries: March 9\, 2026\n\nAn Abstract Vision celebrates the work of artists
  creating abstract art.\n\nAbstract art moves beyond representation\, with
  a strong emphasis on shape\, color and form. Abstract art has the power t
 o evoke emotions\, appeal to our senses and transcend the physical world. 
 Abstract expression captures the delicate\, elusive\, powerful and radiant
  energies that fly under the radar of explanation.\n\nWe are excited to ha
 ve you share with us your visions in the abstract and look forward to putt
 ing together a dynamic exhibition of work that reflects the power and impo
 rtance of abstract art.\n\nAccepting the following mediums: painting\, pri
 ntmaking\, photographs\, sculpture\, glass\, wood\, ceramics\, fiber and p
 aper.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Center for the Arts
URL:https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/an-abstract-vision/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
