BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://museumsc.org/events/?eid=12786"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Conversation with Dr. Caroline Collins and Dr. Raquell Holmes
DTSTART;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260305T170000
DTEND;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260305T190000
UID:260227u2rnJNGixEK5JsZedzPEPA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special evening with Dr. Caroline Collins\, cura
 tor of *Take Me to the Water: Histories of the Black Pacific*. Dr. Collin
 s will be in conversation with Raquell Holmes\, Ph.D. — scientist\, educ
 ator\, and founder of improvscience — sharing insights into the exhibiti
 on's themes\, curatorial process\, and the remarkable stories behind the e
 xhibition. Conversation will be followed by an audience Q&A.\n\n*Take Me t
 o the Water* expands the history of America's maritime past to include th
 e Black whalers\, mariners\, fishers\, explorers\, and sailors who shaped 
 the Pacific Coast from the 16th century to the present day. On view throug
 h March 22\, 2026.\n\nReserve your ticket now!
LOCATION:Museum of Sonoma County
URL:https://museumsc.org/events/?eid=12786
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
