SUMMARY: Oil Portrait in Four Steps with Maggie Parr
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Maggie Parr\nThursday mornings from February 19th
 -March12th\n10:00 am-1:00 pm\n$225 + materials\nLimited to 10 students (f
 irst 4 students to register get a free ½ hour private consult with\nMaggi
 e)\n\nOil painting doesn’t have to be intimidating! In just four weeks\, 
 students will paint a portrait in the indirect style\, starting with a gr
 ey value study\, building up with layers\, and finishing with powerful de
 tails. The final result always surprises people: just by following basic 
 rules\, anyone can create a beautiful oil portrait that glows. Even abstr
 act\npainters can benefit from learning these techniques. Knowing how oil
  painting works give us more confidence to develop our own authentic crea
 tive voice. As Maggie says\, “You gotta learn the rules to break the rule
 s.”\n\n\nMaggie Parr started her career destroying Lichtenstein prints th
 at didn’t make the edition at Gemini G.E.L.\, where she learned that the 
 behemoth art market would not be conducive to her spiritual and personal 
 paintings. She started working as a show designer at Walt Disney Imaginee
 ring\, where for the next three decades\, she designed theme park attract
 ions around the world. She also expanded into book illustration\, murals\
 , portraits\,\ncomics\, and eventually\, writing books and scripts for te
 levision. Along the way\, she studied with master teachers like Steve Hus
 ton\, Jeremy Lipking\, and\nJoseph Q. Daily. She spent years experimentin
 g to find her own creative voice—a fusion of expressionism and realism. S
 he got an MFA and taught at the college level\, then developed her own te
 aching methods for private and group study.\n\nToday\, Maggie maintains a
  thriving business creating custom art and designs for corporations\, ind
 ividuals\, and non-profits. She teaches other artists to utilize classica
 l rendering techniques so they can confidently break the rules in the ser
 vice of their own\nwork. And she coaches creatives in search of deeper au
 thenticity\, healing\, and self- actualization.\n\nPlease follow the link
  to register for this class https://www.parrcreate.com/page/676799 www.pa
 rrcreate.com/page/691159 https://www.parrcreate.com/page/691159 https://w
 ww.parrcreate.com/page/691159
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,Oil-Paint,Painting
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/640bcf85795edf
 4fa3769ae5/68cdced58471971aac0f5188/scaled_384.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:Instructor: Maggie Parr Thursday mornings from Febru
 ary 19th-March12th 10:00 am-1:00 pm $225 + materials Limited to 10 studen
 ts (first 4 students to register...
LOCATION:Rileystreet Art Supply\,103 Maxwell Ct\, Santa Rosa\, CA 95401\,
  USA
CREATED:20260208T191713Z
DTSTAMP:20260303T095337Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260208T232335Z
