UID:260219vcC_3OqnSkiyfAXSX2lD5A
DESCRIPTION:Monsieur Hulot\, Jacques Tati’s endearing clown\, takes a ho
 liday at a seaside resort\, where his presence provokes one catastrophe af
 ter another. Tati’s masterpiece of gentle slapstick is a series of effor
 tlessly well-choreographed sight gags involving dogs\, boats\, and firecra
 ckers\; it was the first entry in the Hulot series and the film that launc
 hed its maker to international stardom. \\(1953\, 87 min\, in French w/Eng
 lish subtitles\\)\n\nFilm - Programmed by Eleanor Nichols\n\nTHE 222 / 222
  Healdsburg Avenue / Healdsburg CA
