SUMMARY:Boeing Boeing - The Play
DESCRIPTION:The play is set in the 1960s\, and centers on bachelor Bernar
 d\, who has a flat in Paris and three airline stewardesses all engaged to
  him without knowing about each other.  Bernard's life gets bumpy\, thoug
 h\, when his friend Robert comes to stay\, and complications such as weat
 her and a new\, speedier Boeing jet disrupt his careful planning. Soon\, 
 all three stewardesses are in the city simultaneously and catastrophe loo
 ms.  By Marc Camoletti  Translated by Beverley Cross and Francis EvansRec
 ommendations: Mild language and innuendo. Recommended for ages 13 and up.
   &#160\;  Location: Frank Chong Studio Theatre in Burbank Auditorium on 
 Santa Rosa Campus.  Tickets: $15 - $25Buy tickets here! (https://srjc.uni
 versitytickets.com/w/event.aspx?SeriesID=31)  SRJC Theatre Arts Website: 
 https://theatrearts.santarosa.edu/ (https://theatrearts.santarosa.edu/)
