SUMMARY:March Month of Flowers Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260306T000000
DTEND;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260306T120000
UID:2602190zJaekOw80-yjOgxzIN5oQ
DESCRIPTION:**Starting March 1st begins the "March Month of Flowers Challe
 nge" (online).** \n\nYou'll receive a list of prompts for every day in Mar
 ch. \n\nCreate an art piece related to the prompt.\n\nShare in our privat
 e Facebook group.\n\nBe inspired and give inspiration to others.\n\n**Only
  $5**\, so everyone can join and share in this creative adventure!\n\n***M
 arch Month of Flowers* Challenge** is here to give you a creative outlet
 \, some structure\, and respite from your brain. \n\nWhen you pick up a b
 rush\, pen\, or pencil (thread\, clay\, fabric…)\, your brain gets a res
 t and becomes more alive and flexible. The world around you becomes more 
 alive\; you pick up on shades\, details\, and patterns all around you. Y
 our intuition gets stronger. And fear lessens\, anxiety fades\, and curios
 ity grows. You stop worrying about making mistakes\, and instead\, you fi
 nd the freedom to simply create
URL:https://www.taradickinson.com/project-page/workshops
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/jizo-peace-project-clay-gathering-mar"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Jizo Peace Project: Clay Gathering — Sebastopol Center For the A
 rts\, California
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260306T000000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260307T000000
UID:ff8a318bbc95d217972db9fffb28f3fa@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Jizo Peace Project: Clay Gathering for Remembrance and Peace\,
  Mar\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $10.00\n        \n      \n  
   \n  \n\nFriday\, March 6\, 2026\; 1:30 – 4:00pmDue to limited capacity
 \, we are asking for a suggested donation of $10 to confirm your attendanc
 e. Bring a copy of your receipt at check-in to Painting/Drawing Studio adj
 acent to Ceramics StudioJoin us for a monthly\, heart-centered gathering w
 here we come together to create Jizo guardians out of clay—symbols of co
 mpassion\, protection\, and peace. Rooted in the Buddhist tradition and ec
 hoed across many cultures\, Jizo figures traditionally honor children and 
 all who have passed\, those in transition\, and those in distress.This ong
 oing project is dedicated to remembering those lost to war\, with a specia
 l focus now on the approximately 19\,000 children who have perished in Isr
 ael and Gaza in recent years. Through the simple\, meditative act of worki
 ng with clay\, we create benevolent beings that will become part of public
  exhibits and peace sites\, offering spaces for reflection\, mourning\, an
 d hope. Our gatherings conclude with a gentle ritual to honor the lives of
  these children.Located in the Painting & Drawing Room. The gathering is o
 pen to ages 12 - adult\, and no prior clay experience is necessary—all c
 lay and basic materials are supplied. Registration is required to particip
 ate.Donations are welcome to help cover materials and expenses. More than 
 a class\, this is a shared space of warmth and care—an opportunity to te
 nd to our own hearts while taking part in love in action.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        \n          \n   
          \n              Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/jizo-peace-project-clay-gathe
 ring-mar
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
