BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/art-of-bookmaking/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Introduction to the Art of Bookmaking
DTSTART;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260306T100000
DTEND;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260306T130000
UID:260124UVRLtCRdEUGk3s2sjmV0Ig
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nFridays\, February 20 – March 13\, 2026 10:00 AM
  – 1:00 PM\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Categories: Fiber 
 Arts\, Other\, Printmaking\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\n$220 – Regis
 tration Cost $30 – Materials Fee $250 – Total Registration CostLearn e
 ssential bookbinding techniques in this 4-week introduction to book arts. 
 Create zines\, pamphlets\, accordion folds\, and more using traditional pa
 per-folding and stitching methods.\n\nWhat you’ll do\n\nJoin guest artis
 t\, Bettina Pauly in this incredible introduction to book arts! The art of
  bookmaking\, otherwise known as bookbinding\, is the physical craft of cr
 eating an artistic book from start to finish. In this introductory 4-sessi
 on class\, you will learn the basic use of bookbinding tools and materials
 \, along with simple bookbinding structures that utilize paper softcovers.
  Students will learn several basic bookbinding structures and stitches tha
 t every beginning book artist should know! Experience technical skills suc
 h as paper folding\, cutting\, sewing and gluing\, mixed with artistic ele
 ments of design to create functional\, elegant objects built for storytell
 ing. The instructor will offer guided instruction in a supportive learning
  environment with a limited class size. Each 3-hour session will meet for 
 four consecutive weeks and focus on the following core bookbinding techniq
 ues:\n\nSession 1: Intro to tools and paper folding\; one sheet wonder zin
 e\, ‘pants’ fold with and without cover\, map folds\n\nSession 2: Pamp
 hlets\, and Japanese stab hole binding\; three hole pamphlet stitch\, five
  hole pamphlet stitch\, Japanese stab binding two holes / five holes \n\n
 Session 3: Accordion folds\; accordion fold\, accordion fold tipped into e
 nvelope cover\, accordion fold with non-adhesive cover\n\nSession 4: Magic
  wallets\, and personal projects\n\nThe class materials fee will include p
 aper and all the tools needed to create each of these projects. Students w
 ill be able to take home all of their book projects at the end of the work
 shop. Please note: This class requires some hand dexterity to maneuver boo
 kbinding tools. Participants should feel comfortable using tools with shar
 p edges such as an awl\, x-acto knife\, and scissors.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/art-of-bookmaking/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/bonsai-and-blossoms/", "Press Democrat": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/bonsai-and-blossoms/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/bonsai-and-blossoms/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Bonsai Show: Bonsai & Blossoms
DTSTART;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260306T100000
DTEND;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260306T170000
UID:260108nAPAKyEdT0iPnjq5IT44cA
DESCRIPTION:January 9–March 22\, 2026\n\nStep into a wonderland of bloom
 ing miniature trees to marvel at the living art of bonsai and the season
 ’s first flowers. Then stroll through our Asian Woodland to admire maje
 stic magnolias\, cherries\, and camellias in bloom\, or join a tour or pro
 gram to explore this timeless craft.\n\nThis year’s all-new presentation
  by the skilled artisans of the Redwood Empire Bonsai Society \\(REBS\\) h
 ighlights the grace and vitality of flowering bonsai—trees and shrubs tr
 ained to bloom in exquisite proportion to their diminutive scale. Delicate
  plum\, azalea\, camellia\, cherry\, and apricot bonsai take center stag
 e\, their blossoms appearing just as winter begins to yield to spring. The
 se early bloomers symbolize hope and renewal—reminding us that beauty an
 d resilience can emerge even in the coldest months.\n\nThe exhibition also
  draws inspiration from hanami\, the centuries-old Japanese tradition of 
 celebrating the fleeting beauty of blossoms. The Garden invites visitors t
 o participate in this art of flower appreciation through Hanami Strolls
 —guided walks through the Garden’s Asian woodland where early-blooming
  magnolias\, cherries\, and camellias offer their own ephemeral display.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/bonsai-and-blossoms/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.sebarts.org/thiebaud"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Unknown Wayne Thiebaud: Passionate Printmaker
DTSTART;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260306T100000
DTEND;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260306T160000
UID:251217VajO8YHQO06pa04oDKxG6A
DESCRIPTION:Wayne Thiebaud's lushly painted still life's of cakes\, pies\,
  and gumball machines are icons of modern American Art. But there is anoth
 er large body of Thiebaud's art that is relatively unknown: his prints. Th
 iebaud had a life-long passion for printmaking --- his first print was mad
 e of pieces of linoleum he ran through the wringer of his mother's washing
  machine! And he continued making prints until well into his 90s. This exh
 ibition will highlight Thiebaud's printed artwork spanning 6 decades\, exp
 loring common themes and subject matter and the artist's unusual working m
 ethod. In addition\, the exhibition will focus on Thiebaud's extraordinary
  relationship with his New York gallerist Allan Stone. Stone gave Thiebaud
  his first major exhibition and continued to represent him for over 45 yea
 rs\, a legendary relationship in the art world. Also join us for a wrap-ar
 ound program lecture on Thursday\, January 29th\, 2026 to hear Wayne Thieb
 aud: The Whole Story from Linda Loveland Reid\, an OLLI instructor for Son
 oma State and Dominican Universities. In this lecture\, we will be discuss
 ing Wayne Thieband's versatile and dynamic personality who brough us not o
 nly delicious dessert paintings\, but also landscapes and figures. In this
  discussion\, we will look at his famous works\, review his life\, and lea
 rn about his extraordinary printmaking skills that are highlighted in the 
 SebArts exhibit. General Admission Tickets are $15.00. Free Public Entry D
 ays Are January 23rd and 24th\, and February 21st and 22nd. SebArts Member
 s are granted free entry\, and students get $5 off per ticket. Purchase yo
 ur tickets before the event\, or at the door. To schedule a docent led gro
 up tour of 6 or more\, email RWynne@sebarts.org.\n\nDate and Time: Saturda
 y January 10\, 2026 at 10:00 am to Sunday March 8\, 2026 at 4:00 pm
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center For The Arts
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/thiebaud
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/big-and-small-pinching-pots/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Big and Small\; Pinching Pots with Dan Clauson
DTSTART;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260306T100000
DTEND;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260306T130000
UID:2512080IZ_Ddi6q0ehILD7TTKymw
DESCRIPTION:Fridays\, January 30 – March 13\, 2026 10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\
 n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Categories: Art Departments\, C
 eramics\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n17\\+\n\n$230 Registration Fee $30 Materials Fee 
 $260 Total Registration Fee\n\nA class that is all about pinching! With in
 structor Dan\, students will learn handbuilding methods to coil and pitch 
 their vessels. With specific direction in learning the techniques to build
  any size of pot\, from a large scale vessel to a small cup. We will learn
  how to support scaling up our forms through drying methods\, interior ‘
 bone’ structure\, and mastering directionality with our hands. There wil
 l be a focus on how we each make a mark upon a pot\, and how to do so with
  purpose. Each student will create work that reflects the time-honored nat
 ure of handbuilding\; when intention is given to the silhouette of a form\
 , the lip of a cup\, and/or the comfort of a handle. Each class will invol
 ve a warmup\, a demo\, and worktime. Most classes will have \\(fun&thought
 ful\\) homework.\n\nRequired Class Supply List\n\nYou can view the require
 s class supply list here.\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/big-and-small-pinching-pots
 /
