X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/rooted-and-rising-honoring-the-lineage-of-women-in-buddhism-mg1b26/?lang=en", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/rooted-and-rising-honoring-the-lineage-of-women-in-buddhism/18115046/2026-03-07T10"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/rooted-and-rising-honoring-the-lineage-of-women-in-buddhism-mg1b26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Rooted and Rising: Honoring the Lineage of Women in Buddhism
DTSTART;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260307T100000
DTEND;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260307T130000
UID:2602145xH_5g9B7kOk1kat9VwBOQ
DESCRIPTION:with Kate Munding\, Jennifer Berezan\, DaRa Williams and Erin 
 Treat\n\nAcross centuries and continents\, women have deep roots in the Bu
 ddha Dharma. They have been great contributors and carriers of the lineage
  and yet have too often remained hidden beneath the surface of history. Th
 eir stories are fierce\, resilient\, and revolutionary. Do you know them?\
 n\nFrom the first Buddhist nuns who challenged the norms of their time\, t
 o modern-day teachers\, mothers\, activists\, and visionaries reshaping sp
 iritual life today\, women have always been keystones to the continuation 
 of the Dharma. This benefit event invites all genders to step into that le
 gacy—to see\, honor\, and draw strength from the women who have shaped t
 he Dharma with their courage and uncompromising truth.\n\nTogether with an
  inspiring group of contemporary Dharma teachers\, we’ll explore these s
 tories and ask: What guidance do these spiritual ancestors offer us now—
 when clarity\, groundedness\, and collective courage are so urgently neede
 d?
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/rooted-and-rising-hono
 ring-the-lineage-of-women-in-buddhism-mg1b26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
