X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://napavalleymuseum.org/products/au-revoir-julia-at-the-mac", "Press Democrat": "https://napavalleymuseum.org/products/au-revoir-julia-at-the-mac"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://napavalleymuseum.org/products/au-revoir-julia-at-the-mac"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:"Au Revoir\, Julia" at The MAC
DTSTART;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260307T130000
DTEND;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260307T160000
UID:260225kVQvnBnXSkGqwbT6TpHySA
DESCRIPTION:Take a last look at Julia with a free event at The MAC featu
 ring **Bella Union Winery**\, on the final weekend of our inaugural e
 xhibition: “**Julia Child: A Recipe for Life”** \n\nDate: Saturday\,
  March 7\, 2026 Time: 1-4 p.m. Location: The Napa Valley Museum of Art
  & Culture (The MAC)  \n\nJoin us for a warm and welcoming afternoon as
  we partner with **Bella Union Winery** for a special farewell tribute
  event. Enjoy a selection of exceptional wines by Bella Union Winery in c
 elebration of Julia Child and her joyful approach to life\, and browse 
 the museum store at no charge.  Enjoy special discounts on select Ju
 lia Child inspired merchandise. **Purchase tickets** to experience 
 “**Julia Child: A Recipe for Life\,”** an immersive exhibition celebr
 ating the iconic chef and broadcasting pioneer. The wine tasting is open 
 to all visitors 21+\n\nIt’s hard to believe that our first exhibition a
 t The MAC is coming to its end\, but our national tour of "Julia Child
 : A Recipe for Life" continues. The exhibition officially closes March
  8\, 2026\, at 5 PM. Come raise a glass with us and celebrate\, Julia 
 Child\, whose legacy continues to inspire.
LOCATION:The MAC
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/products/au-revoir-julia-at-the-mac
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.facebook.com/events/900222262926990/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:We are Proud to Present a Presentation about the Herero of Namibia
DTSTART;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260307T130000
DTEND;TZID=PST;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260307T150000
UID:260303P7rf7oLkaEivkAek1gLBTA
DESCRIPTION:We are Proud to Present... Written by Jackie Sibblies Drury Fe
 bruary 20-March 8\, 2026 Director Skylar Evans A powerful\, meta-theatrica
 l examination of race\, history\, and storytelling. Six actors attempt to 
 portray the genocide of the Herero people by German colonizers—but what 
 begins as rehearsal quickly descends into a confrontation of privilege\, p
 erspective\, and the uncomfortable truths of performance itself. Lexus Fle
 tcher – Actor 6/Black Woman Thomas Peterson – Actor 1/White Man Isiah 
 Carter – Actor 2/Black Man Nate Musser – Actor 3/Another White Man Sam
  Minnifield – Actor 4/Another Black Man Maddi Scarbrough – Actor 5/Sar
 ah Mercedes Murphy – \\(U/S\\) Actor 6/Black Woman Wed\, Thur\, Fri and 
 Sat nights at 7:30pm. Sat and Sun matinees at 1pm
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/900222262926990/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
