BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup: Go Wild Hikers": "https://www.meetup.com/sonoma-county-go-wild-hikers/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_go_wild_hikers
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Go Wild Hikers
URL:https://www.meetup.com/sonoma-county-go-wild-hikers/
UID:event_313345254@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260303T213749Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260308T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260308T123000
SUMMARY:Bothe Napa Valley State Park
DESCRIPTION:Go Wild Hikers\nSpring is almost here. **Daylight Savings Time
  Begins**\n**Set your clocks Ahead One Hour or you'll miss the hike.** Joi
 n us for a hike in Napa Valley. Bothe is 1900 acres of beautiful redwoods\
 , bay laurel\, madrones and moss-covered Douglas fir\, orchids\, trilliums
  and wildflowers (in season)\, spotted owls\, pileated woodpeckers and for
 est pigeons\, springs\, creeks and ferns. You will not be disappointed! A 
 challenging hike\, best for individuals with at least a moderate level of 
 fitness.\n\n**Where We Meet/Directions**\nBothe Napa Valley State Park\n38
 01 St. Helena Hwy (Highway 29/128)\, Calistoga\, CA 94515\nThe park is loc
 ated approximately 5 miles north of St. Helena and 4 miles south of Calist
 oga on Highway 29/128.\nAfter passing the **entrance & Pay Station** follo
 w the road to a large parking area. There are bathrooms past this parking 
 lot about 200 yards.\nGive yourself plenty of time to arrive\, pay park fe
 e and use the toilet. It often takes longer than you think.\n\n**After Hik
 e Gathering?**\nThe Calistoga Creamery\n1473 Lincoln Avenue\, Calistoga 94
 515\nhttps://www.yelp.com/biz/calistoga-creamery-calistoga\nAn outstanding
  ice cream shop! Opens at 12 pm Sat and Sun.\nOrganic ice cream and organi
 c frozen yogurt\, thick custom milk shakes\, root beer floats and sundaes.
  No high fructose corn syrup\, artificial colors or flavors. No hydrogenat
 ed oils and no GMOs.\n\n**Group Hike #334**\nCoyote Peak Trail to Ritchey 
 Canyon Trail - A loop hike\nDistance - 6 miles/9.7 kilometers\nElevation c
 hange - 1100 feet/335 meters\nDifficulty - 7+ out of 10 - moderate\nExposu
 res - 20 % sun/ 80% shade- rocky\, creek crossings\, mud\, poison oak\, ti
 cks & insects.\nBring plenty of water. At least 68 oz./2 liters\nDogs - No
 t permitted\nFacilities at trail head - Shade\, picnic table\, restrooms d
 own the road.\nCost - $5 cash\nParking - State Parks fee of $8 or free wit
 h your State Park Pass.\nRemember to wear appropriate hiking shoes\, bring
  plenty of water\, a hat\, a snack/lunch and layered clothing.\nPlease Do 
 Not Use Any scented products the day of a group hike!\nOf course\, we will
  all look out for each other but ultimately\, hikers are responsible for t
 heir own safety and well-being during hikes.\n\n**When We Meet**\nSunday M
 arch 8\, 2026\n**Daylight Savings Time Begins**\n**Set your clocks Ahead O
 ne Hour or you'll miss the hike.**\n9:00 am - 12:30 pm PDT\nIf your plans 
 change after you sign up even if you're on the waitlist\, please update yo
 ur RSVP.\nDo Not Attend if you are sick\, running a fever\, were exposed t
 o or have tested positive for Covid-19 or any other contagion!\nHike may b
 e changed\, rescheduled or cancelled in case of excessive heat\, rain\, sm
 oke/AQI\, illness\, zombie apocalypse etc... Check your email the night be
 fore for any possible changes.\n\n**Notice to New Hikers Only**\n**"When a
  New Hiker (never hiked with me before) doesn't show up (No Show) to their
  first hike with the group\, they will be removed (not banned) from the gr
 oup immediately."**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/sonoma-county-go-wild-hikers/events/3
 13345254/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260213T191723Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260213T191723Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
