SUMMARY:"Champagne Girl in a Budweiser Family" Author Reading with Suzanne
  Weerts
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260308T120000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260308T140000
UID:260227pXnEjWICbUqmu6KZbYV3oA
DESCRIPTION:Champagne Girl in a Budweiser Family by Suzanne Weerts is a fu
 nny and touching memoir told through vivid\, story-driven moments of growi
 ng up in the American South in the 1970’s and ’80’s. With warmth and
  sharp humor\, Weerts explores class\, culture\, and family expectations 
 — what it’s like to be a girl with champagne tastes in a Budweiser fam
 ily\, and how those early contradictions shape a life. Suzanne will be doi
 ng a book event March 8 in Healdsburg at the Healdsburg Bubble Bar. The bo
 ok balances laugh-out-loud observations with genuine emotional depth and w
 ill appeal to readers who enjoy character-driven memoirs about women\, fam
 ily\, and identity. Please join us!
LOCATION:Healdsburg Bubble Bar
URL:http://www.healdsburgbubblebar.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
