SUMMARY:Boeing Boeing - The Play
DESCRIPTION:The play is set in the 1960s\, and centers on bachelor Bernar
 d\, who has a flat in Paris and three airline stewardesses all engaged to
  him without knowing about each other.  Bernard's life gets bumpy\, thoug
 h\, when his friend Robert comes to stay\, and complications such as weat
 her and a new\, speedier Boeing jet disrupt his careful planning. Soon\, 
 all three stewardesses are in the city simultaneously and catastrophe loo
 ms.  By Marc Camoletti  Translated by Beverley Cross and Francis EvansRec
 ommendations: Mild language and innuendo. Recommended for ages 13 and up.
   &#160\;  Location: Frank Chong Studio Theatre in Burbank Auditorium on 
 Santa Rosa Campus.  Tickets: $15 - $25Buy tickets here! (https://srjc.uni
 versitytickets.com/w/event.aspx?SeriesID=31)  SRJC Theatre Arts Website: 
 https://theatrearts.santarosa.edu/ (https://theatrearts.santarosa.edu/)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The play is set in the 1960s\, and cent
 ers on bachelor Bernard\, who has a flat in Paris and three airline stewa
 rdesses all engaged to him without knowing about each other.<br />  Berna
 rd's life gets bumpy\, though\, when his friend Robert comes to stay\, an
 d complications such as weather and a new\, speedier Boeing jet disrupt h
 is careful planning. Soon\, all three stewardesses are in the city simult
 aneously and catastrophe looms.</p><p>  By Marc Camoletti<br />  Translat
 ed by Beverley Cross and Francis Evans<br /><strong>Recommendations:</str
 ong> Mild language and innuendo. Recommended for ages 13 and up.</p><p>  
 &#160\;</p><p>  Location: Frank Chong Studio Theatre in Burbank Auditoriu
 m on Santa Rosa Campus.</p><p>  Tickets: $15 - $25</p><p><a href="https:/
 /srjc.universitytickets.com/w/event.aspx?SeriesID=31" target="_blank" rel
 ="noopener">Buy tickets here!</a></p><p>  SRJC Theatre Arts Website: <a h
 ref="https://theatrearts.santarosa.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">h
 ttps://theatrearts.santarosa.edu/</a></p>
