BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/book-reading-shah-razad-and-the-djins-who-lover-her-with-author-jazzmyn-inisis"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Book reading: Shah Razad and the Djins Who Lover Her with author J
 azzmyn Inisis
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260308T160000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260308T173000
UID:251229NzwSqlyLvE2ZlrRA187__g
DESCRIPTION:Jazzmyn Inisis will read from her book\, Shah Razad and the Dj
 ins Who Loved Her in the OCA lobby. Jazzmyn is a local writer who was deep
 ly influenced living in the middle east as a child of a military father st
 ationed there in the 1950's. Join us for an afternoon of mystery and story
 telling with Jazzmyn\, accompanied by middle eastern food and fine wines a
 vailable for purchase. Settle in and be transported! Free admission\, all 
 donations happily accepted.   She writes "I am nine years old living in Da
 macus\, Syria. My father is on a diplomatic assignment with the United Nat
 ions to ease tensions on the volatile border between Jordan and Israel. We
  are transferred from Damacus\, Syria\, to Jerusalem\, Jordan in late 1955
 . I came to know and love my Bedouin neighbors. They kindly lend me their 
 only donkey. I attend their daughter's wedding and join their family in th
 e Suk to shop in the inner city of Jerusalem. I am envious of their beauti
 ful\, embroidered dresses and have fallen deeply in love with my kind and 
 generous neighbors. Ten years ago\, I picked up volume number one of "The 
 Book of the Thousand Nights and One Night" translated by Sir Richard Franc
 is Burton. The first of sixteen volumes of the stories Shah Razad told her
  emperor over one thousand nights in order to curtail his slaughter of eve
 ry young\, noble woman in her country. After completing the sixteen volume
 s of "Shah Razad" i felt compelled to continue this extraordinary traditio
 n of storytelling\, intended to transmit moral values\, by adding my own s
 tory: Shah Razad...and the Djinns Who Loved Her.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/book-readin
 g-shah-razad-and-the-djins-who-lover-her-with-author-jazzmyn-inisis
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayoa.org/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.northbayoa.org/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayoa.org/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting in Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260308T160000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260308T170000
UID:260212ikY6_Lv3kk6VcjZmeLgJMQ
DESCRIPTION:**Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.**\n\nOvereater
 s Anonymous (OA) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits.\n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on **Sunda
 ys from 4:00 – 5:00 PM** **at Christ Church United Methodist\, 1717 Yulu
 pa Ave.\, Room #4\, Santa Rosa**. Contact: Abigail (707) 293-5888. You may
  view all North Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northb
 ayoa.org/meetings.html .\n\nIn OA\, members experience **spiritual\, emoti
 onal\, and physical recovery** by practicing the **Twelve Steps** and livi
 ng by their spiritual principles—one day at a time.\n\nOA is **not** a d
 iet club or calorie-counting program.\n\nMembers have different plans of e
 ating.\n\nOA does **not** endorse any specific food plan.\n\nIf food is ca
 using problems in your life\, you don’t have to struggle alone. Recovery
  is possible\, and help is available.\n\n**Visit:** https://www.northbayoa
 .org/\n\n**Find a meeting:** https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Christ Church United Methodist
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
