DESCRIPTION:Mondays\, January 5 – MAdvance your oil painting skills in a
  supportive\, solvent-free studio while exploring color\,arch 9\, 2026 9:3
 0 AM – 12:30 PM No class January 19 and February 16\n\nExperience Level\
 n\nIntermediate and Advanced\n\nEvent Category: Drawing & Painting\n\nAge\
 \(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\n$350 – Registration Cost $35 – Optional Mate
 rials Packet\n\nAdvance your oil painting skills in a supportive\, solvent
 -free studio while exploring color\,light\, and challenging subjects to de
 epen technique and expression.\n\nWhat you’ll do\n\nThis 8-week course i
 s designed for artists ready to deepen their technical skills and personal
  expression in a calm\, supportive\, and solvent-free studio. It serves as
  the natural continuation of the Fall 2025 course “Palette & Possibility
 \,” and is also open to experienced oil painters who wish to advance the
 ir practice within a framework focused on cognitive stimulation and emotio
 nal well-being. We will move beyond simple objects to tackle subjects that
  introduce new cognitive challenges\, such as atmosphere\, reflective surf
 aces\, and simplified portrait elements. Emphasis remains on process over 
 product\, nurturing focus\, spatial reasoning\, and emotional insight. Thr
 ough an explorative journey into composition\, light\, and “The Chromati
 c Voice”—your unique use of color— students will strengthen their ar
 tistic voices while continuing to reap the rewards of enhanced mental agil
 ity and profound emotional well-being.\n\nOptional Materials Packet & Supp
 ly List\n\n$35 includes all necessary paints\, mediums\, brushes\, surface
