BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/the-seasons-dance-on-ice?aff=cityspark"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Seasons - Dance on Ice
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260313T190000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260313T200000
UID:2602271XJNqoG6GEuqHnN4PE0nAw
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Snoopy's Home Ice for an evening of art and athleti
 cism of Dance on Ice.\n\nSnoopy's Home Ice\n\nMarch 13th 2026 at 7PM\n\nOl
 ympic Champion Gabriella Papadakis leads Ice Dance International's new tou
 r\, THE SEASONS&mdash\;a celebration of artistry\, athleticism\, and speed
  that turns the rink into a living stage. Papadakis joins 2-time United St
 ates Champion Alissa Czisny and skating artist Rohene Ward in a company of
  ten world class skaters. From the opening movement they shape formations 
 that move through four acts\; each sharing a story that takes the audience
  on a journey.\n\nTHE SEASONS bursts with color\, emotion\, and momentum. 
  Ice Dance International company members launch daring lifts and jumps\, c
 risp footwork\, and seamless transitions that thrilled audiences on IDI's 
 2025 tour.\n\nPapadakis\, Czisny and Ward's presence elevates every phrase
 &mdash\;their power\, musical instinct\, and magnetic connection ignite th
 e audience and sharpen the edge of every moment. This is skating unbound: 
 athletic\, cinematic\, and wildly alive.\n\nReaching 14 cities in early 20
 26\, this is the rare chance to witness the possibilities of performance d
 ance on ice. IDI's Artistic Director Douglas Webster says &ldquo\;THE SEAS
 ONS isn't just a show&mdash\;it's a pulse\, a spark\, a reminder that when
  blades meet music and movement meets heart\, the ice itself begins to sin
 g.&rdquo\; \n\nEdge Class details: The edge class are meant to be communit
 y events that allow an opportunity to skate and warm up with the IDI compa
 ny. Skills required are a solid ability of forwards and backwards skating/
 cross overs\, all basic edges and turns through forward and backward 3s. C
 lasses will develop past 3 turns into more advanced exercises. Both youth 
 and adults are welcome. These classes are not learn to skate classes and a
 dvance at a rapid pace.\n\nMeet and Greets follow the show and are a chanc
 e for VIP ticket holders to get autographs and photos with the IDI cast me
 mbers. It generally take the cast 25 minutes to finish a show\, regroup an
 d get to the meet and greet! There will be flyers and markers for signing.
  \n\n \n\n 
LOCATION:Snoopy's Home Ice
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/the-seasons-dance-on-ice?a
 ff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-menagerie/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-menagerie/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-menagerie/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Glass Menagerie
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260313T193000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260313T213000
UID:260227lBBX3kVCCkuPAnhgucbVvA
DESCRIPTION:The 2026 Season at Curtain Call Theatre starts off with **The 
 Glass Menagerie**\, the play that made Tennessee Williams famous.\n\nHave 
 You Ever Felt Stuck Between Your Dreams and Reality? This Play Gets It.\n\
 nImagine being trapped in a tiny apartment during the Great Depression —
  no money\, no way out\, just a family clinging to hopes that may never co
 me true. That's exactly what The Glass Menagerie is about.\n\nWritten by T
 ennessee Williams — one of America's greatest playwrights — this story
  follows a restless son\, an overbearing mom\, and a painfully shy daughte
 r as they each chase dreams that feel just out of reach. It's emotional\, 
 poetic\, and honestly… kind of hits different when you think about your 
 own life.\n\nThis iconic play is literally studied in classrooms worldwide
 \, so seeing it live is like watching your textbook come to life — excep
 t way more powerful.\n\n📅 March 13–29\, 2026\n\n📍 20347 Hwy 116\, 
 Monte Rio\, CA\n\n🎟️ Grab your tickets at russianriverhall.com or cal
 l (707) 387-5072\n\nThe Glass Menagerie by Tennessee Williams is directed 
 by Michael Tabib.\n\nShowing at the Russian River Hall in Monte Rio\, CA f
 rom March 13-29\, 2026.\n\nProgram was made possible\, in part\, with fund
 s from Creative Sonoma and the California Arts Council (CAC).\n\nBy specia
 l arrangement with Dramatists Play Services\, Inc.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-mena
 gerie/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/indie-after-dark/16448446/2026-03-13T19"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Indie After Dark
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260313T193000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260313T230000
UID:260106aKrHhpLmE0WxVh1wcVJkmw
DESCRIPTION:Indie After Dark – Vallejo’s Night for Original Music\n\nS
 eptember 12 performers:\n\n🔥 Agness Twin\n\nSan Francisco’s hypnotic 
 post-punk / indie project led by Elisa Ovrahim. Gorgeous layered vocals\, 
 ringing guitars\, cinematic folk shadows\, and minimalist ethereal pop. Th
 eir new album Turn To Gold \\(2024\\) was mastered by John Golden \\(Sound
 garden\, Melvins\\) and has already carved its place on indie radio. Fresh
  from the Love & Rockets tour\, Agness Twin’s live set will swallow you 
 whole.\n\n🔥 Pro-Pain!\n\nBay Area 4-piece that’s “HAVING A BLAST.
 ” High-voltage energy\, pure grit\, and a sound built to light up the ro
 om. With their recent Bombs Away video\, they’re proof that Vallejo’s 
 underground scene is very much alive and screaming.\n\nEvery Second Friday
 \, Indie After Dark brings the spotlight to independent music at the intim
 ate and vibey 4th Corner Speakeasy in downtown Vallejo. Just steps from th
 e heart of the Vallejo Art Walk\, this monthly series invites you to disco
 ver bold new sounds in a setting made for connection—where the lights ar
 e low\, the cocktails are strong\, and the music runs deep.\n\nCome early 
 for the art\, stay late for the music. It’s a night where Vallejo’s cr
 eative soul shines.
LOCATION:4th Corner Speakeasy
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/indie-after-dark/164484
 46/2026-03-13T19
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.facebook.com/events/2318855651949065/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Steampunk
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260313T193000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260313T220000
UID:260303M6FdXUdELkSssQJpwdzr9A
DESCRIPTION:Don't miss this show featuring Steampunk fashion and props - b
 ring or wear your own! Qu'in de la Noche makes her premiere appearance at 
 Forbidden Kiss LIVE in this Steampunk-themed show. Cheryl King presents ba
 wdy vaudeville at its finest\, with burlesque from Thotty McNaughty\, and 
 musical performances from Ruby Reprise and Karenna Slade. Titus Androgynou
 s will bring their new drag routine\, and Underground Improv provides come
 dy sketches and improvisation with prompts from the audience. A costume co
 ntest is planned\, with the audience voting for their favorites with our v
