DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260313T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260313T200000
DTSTAMP:20260302T145213
CREATED:20260213T160255Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260213T160255Z
UID:25596-1773432000-1773432000@www.uptowntheatrenapa.com
SUMMARY:Billy Idol Should Be Dead - Movie Screening
DESCRIPTION:March 13\, 2026\nPURCHASE TICKETS HERE  \nDoors 7pm/ Show 8pm\nAges: 12+ \n“Billy Idol Should Be Dead” Debuted at Tribeca followed by Sheffield DocFest. \nBilly Idol Should Be Dead is a feature-length documentary tracing the life and career of the punk pioneer turned rock ‘n’ roll icon. Through never-before-seen archival and personal interviews with Idol\, his family\, peers and collaborators\, the documentary digs deep into Billy Idol’s emergence as a prototypical punk rocker\, his meteoric rise as a global superstar in the MTV era and the myriad of challenges Idol had to overcome to not just survive\, but to remain one of the most beloved figures in rock n roll\, almost fifty years into his career and still selling out arenas around the world. Directed by Jonas Akerlund. \n“[A] harrowing redemption story…the Billy Idol documentary is an excellent and expansively researched two-hour deep dive that traces Idol’s life and career in the familiar ‘Behind the Music’ format\, but with long looks at peak eras and a depth of detail\, both factual and emotional\, that elevate it above that standard.”—Variety \n“[A] wild and surprisingly heartfelt documentary…the film leaves no stone unturned in telling Idol’s improbable story.”—The Ankler \n“a story about survival”—USA Today
URL:https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/event/billy-idol-should-be-dead-movie-screening/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/BI_1920X1005.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107705774?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
