X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup: Go Wild Hikers": "https://www.meetup.com/sonoma-county-go-wild-hikers/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_go_wild_hikers
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Go Wild Hikers
URL:https://www.meetup.com/sonoma-county-go-wild-hikers/
UID:event_313563939@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260303T213749Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260314T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260314T113000
SUMMARY:Valentine Vista at Moore Creek Park
DESCRIPTION:Go Wild Hikers\nJoin me in exploring Moore Creek Park's 1\,600
  acres of rugged terrain including Oak woodlands\, Douglas Fir & Madrone f
 orest\, grasslands\, chaparral and spectacular wildflowers (in season). Wi
 ldlife in the park is plentiful\, including large mammals such as black be
 ars\, mountain lions\, bobcat\, gray fox and coyote. Best for individuals 
 with at least a moderate level of fitness.\n\n**Where We Meet/Important Di
 rections**\nMoore Creek Park\n2602 Chiles Pope Valley Rd\, St Helena\, CA 
 94574\n**Get there Early! Carpool if you can - This is a very Popular Park
 !**\nSouth on Hwy 128 past Calistoga - Left on Deer Park Rd (Sign Pacific 
 Union College) - Right on Silverado Trail - Left on Sage Valley Rd/Hwy 128
  - Past Lake Hennessey - Pay Attention - Left on Chiles Pope Valley Rd - L
 eft into Moore Creek Park past a private house on a very narrow road there
  is a large parking lot.\nGive yourself plenty of time to arrive. It's oft
 en farther than you think.\n\n**The Hike (group hike #335**\nValentine Vis
 ta and Moore Creek trails - A loop hike\nDistance - 4.75 miles/7.64 kilome
 ters\nElevation change - 800 feet/244 meters\nDifficulty - 6 out of 10 - M
 oderately easy\nExposures - 60% sun/40 % shade - poison oak\, ticks/insect
 s and views.\nMust be sure footed (confident and competent)!\nBring plenty
  of water. At least 34 oz./1 liter!\nDogs - No. They are prohibited in Moo
 re Crk (This Hike) and permitted at the Lake Hennessey section (other hike
 s).\nFacilities at trail head - Port O Potti.\nI suggest you stop elsewher
 e.\nCost - $5 cash.\nParking - Free - Napa Ag & Open Space excepts donatio
 ns.\nRemember to wear appropriate hiking shoes\, bring plenty of water\, a
  hat\, a snack/lunch and layered clothing.\nPlease Do Not Use Any scented 
 products the day of a group hike!\nOf course we will all look out for each
  other but ultimately\, hikers are responsible for their own safety and we
 ll-being during hikes.\n\n**After Hike Gathering?**\nBella Bakery & Cafe\n
 1353 Lincoln Avenue Calistoga\, CA 94515\nMonday-Saturday: 6am-2pm\nSunday
 : 7am-2pm\n707-942-1443\nbellabakerycakes@gmail.com\n\n**When We Meet**\nS
 aturday March 14\, 2026\n830 am - 1130 am\n**Get there Early! Carpool if y
 ou can - This is a very Popular Park!**\nIf your plans change after you si
 gn up even if you're on the waitlist\, please update your RSVP.\nDo Not At
 tend if you are sick\, running a fever\, were exposed to or have tested po
 sitive for Covid-19 or any other contagion!\nHike may be postponed or canc
 elled in case of excessive heat\, rain\,\nsmoke/AQI\, illness\, zombie apo
 calypse etc... Check your email the\nnight before for any possible changes
 .\n\n**Notice to New Hikers Only**\n**When a New Hiker (never hiked with m
 e before) doesn't show up (No Show) to their first hike with the group\, t
 hey will be removed (not banned) from the group immediately.**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/sonoma-county-go-wild-hikers/events/3
 13563939/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260227T220512Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260227T220512Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/inthffspring26", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/park-rx-intermediate-hiking-for-fitness/18210471/2026-03-14T09"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/inthffspring26"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Park Rx—Intermediate Hiking for Fitness
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260314T090000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260314T130000
UID:260227ot8h_hxA9EKO1JgcDTkCbQ
DESCRIPTION:If you have previously completed the Beginner Hiking f
 or Fitness Program\, or can hike a little more than 4 miles wi
 th at least 1\,000 ft of elevation\, this hiking series is for
  you! The program leaders will guide you on 8 weekly hikes wit
 h the challenge increasing each week. Leaders will have group di
 scussions about gear\, hydration\, hiking poles\, first aid and p
 acing\, etc. The group's final hike aims for Bald Mountain\, whe
 re hikers can enjoy stunning vistas.\n\nThe following is a list 
 of possible routes specifically selected for this hiking series: 
 \n\n1) Sat 3/7 — Creekside + Waterfall loop\, 3.6 miles\, 750
  ft elevation \\[meet @ White Barn\\] 2) Sat 3/14 – Vista Tra
 il loop\, 3.4 miles\, 830 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Barn\\] 3
 ) Sat 3/21 – Goodspeed to Nattkemper bench\, 3.8 miles\, 1\,24
 0 ft elevation \\[meet @ Goodspeed lot\\] 4) Sat 3/28 – Hillsi
 de to Neptune table + Meadow\, 4.4 miles\, 970 ft elevation \\[
 meet @ White Barn\\] 5) Sat 4/4 – Hillside + Vista Trail loop
 \, 3.6 miles\, 1\,070 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Barn\\] 6) Sa
 t 4/11 – False Lake Meadow & Lake Ilsanjo loop in Trionne-Ann
 adel SP\, 6.1 miles\, 670 ft elevation \\[meet @ Annadel's Cobbl
 estone Trailhead\\] 7) Sat 4/18 – Fern Lake + Orchard loop in
  SDC/Jack London SHP\, 5.5 miles\, 1\,460 ft elevation \\[meet @
  Walnut & North St inside SDC\; park on Grove St\\] 8) Sat 4/2
 5 – Bald Mtn summit (w/optional Headwaters detour\, 5.8 miles)\
 , 5.1 miles\, 1\,670 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Barn\\]\n\nPlea
 se note these routes are subject to change based on the group 
 and weather. Wear appropriate footwear for rocky or slippery trai
 ls\, and layers. Bring water\, and if desired\, a snack. The gr
 oup will be limited to 35 participants. \n\nThe hiking series co
 sts $80 (plus a $10 parking fee per visit. Note that the Sugar
 loaf Annual Pass is $59 and valid at Sugarloaf and Jack London
  SHP)\, or free-of-cost for participants with a January 2025 or
  newer Park Rx from a Sonoma County Medical Provider.  The num
 ber of available Park Rx tickets is limited\; please have your 
 Rx ready at the time of sign up.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/inthffspring26
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
