BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sweetwatermusichall.org/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Wicked Messengers
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260314T200000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260314T233000
UID:260302T4mR6j3gsE2wIZB2AMS6qQ
DESCRIPTION:Rooted in the vibrant Bay Area jam band scene\, **Wicked Mess
 engers** brings a fresh interpretation to the timeless songs of Bob Dylan
 \, Neil Young\, Jerry Garcia\, and more. This collective of seasoned music
 ians embodies a deep respect for famous classic songs while infusing their
  performances with a unique and organic flair.\n\nAt the heart of Wicked M
 essengers are guitarist Pat Nevins\, affectionately known as Shakey Zimmer
 man\, brings his dynamic style and heartfelt vocals\, guitar and harmonica
  to the forefront\; Jay Wilcox\, known for his Garcia esqe guitar tone and
  vocals\, contributes his exceptional prowess\, vocals and harmonies\; mul
 ti-instrumentalist Justin Wooster adds depth with his versatile musiciansh
 ip\, from drums to mandolin and vocals. \n\nThe full electric ensemble cr
 eates a rich tapestry of sound\, enhanced by the driving rhythms of drums\
 , keyboard melodies\, bass lines\, and the soulful twang of pedal steel gu
 itar. For a more intimate experience\, Wicked Messengers also offers a cap
 tivating acoustic trio\, showcasing the intricate interplay of guitars and
  mandolin. The trio unit offers up a vast and deep collection of songs. \
 n\nWicked Messengers made its debut on August 9\, 2025 at Sweetwater Music
  Hall with an amazing 8 band member electric show. That show emerged from 
 an Alcazar Theatre\, Carpinteria CA Shakey Zimmerman show with the additio
 n of guitarist Jay Wilcox resulting in an ongoing project with wide sonic 
 reach. \n\nJoin Wicked Messengers on a musical journey that celebrates th
 e spirit of legendary american songwriters while embracing the improvisati
 onal essence of jam band culture with many of the best Bay Area supporting
  musicians. Get ready for a landscape of songs that honors the past and in
 vigorates the present\, as each performance is a unique experience driven 
 by passion and spontaneity.
LOCATION:Sweetwater Music Hall
URL:https://sweetwatermusichall.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1037960609?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Nate Clark & Charlie Hunter Trio & Marcus Finnie
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260314T200000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260314T000000
UID:260224xnELXRpj40q_7p83ubdMuA
DESCRIPTION:Charlie Hunter \\(born May 23\, 1967\\) is an American guitari
 st\, composer and bandleader.  First coming to prominence in the early '90
 s Hunter has since become one of the leading names in jazz\, recording 17 
 albums. Hunter is noted for playing custom-made seven and eight-string gui
 tars\, on which he simultaneously plays basslines\, rhythm guitar\, and so
 los. Critic Sean Westergaard describes Hunter's innovative guitar techniqu
 e as "mind-boggling ... he's an agile improviser with an ear for great ton
 e\, and always has excellent players alongside him in order to make great 
 music\, not to show off."
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1037960609?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107920196?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Charlie Hunter Trio feat: Marcus Finnie and Nate Clark
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260314T200000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260314T000000
UID:260224WIV1PX0Zs0SCFTwW2-HOgw
DESCRIPTION:Guitar legend Charlie Hunter is widely considered one of the t
 op jazz bandleaders in the United States. As the "hip-hop" or "acid jazz" 
 movement of the mid-1990s gained momentum in the United States\, Charlie H
 unter was leading it in the San Francisco Bay Area. Young groups of avant-
 garde jazz musicians were mixing traditional jazz with hip-hop\, funk\, an
 d rock. Hunter was the first out of the pack of groups of the area to be r
 eleased on CD. "We study the past and practice the present\," Hunter told 
 Down Beat in 1994. That blend of past and present was what Hunter used to 
 push his award-winning trio towards many successful releases and tours. Hi
 s inventive use of a custom guitar earned him astute musicians as fans\, a
 nd his talent for creating infectious hip-hop dance grooves have made Hunt
 er's live shows legendary. Charlie Hunter has release 17 studio albums in 
 the last two decades. Hunter will be joined by Nate Clark on Sax and Marcu
 s Finnie on drums.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107920196?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
