BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.cedarslife.org/events"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:"You're My Neighbor" Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260315T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260315T170000
UID:260227ZEiHVtcn6EGGNe7BZsYsxg
DESCRIPTION:Come out to Point Reyes and celebrate neighbors!   \n\nFrom 
 mooing cows and soaring birds to friendly faces down the road\, Cedars art
 ists take a joyful look at their Marin County neighborhood. This exhibitio
 n explores all the things that make their corner of the world special—op
 en fields\, wild creatures\, familiar people\, and the everyday moments in
  between. Through colorful\, thoughtful\, and imaginative works\, “You
 ’re My Neighbor” celebrates the beauty of living side by side and shar
 ing a place we call home.\n\n​Cedars “You’re My Neighbor!” art exh
 ibition runs from March 3 through April 12\, 2026
LOCATION:Toby's Feed Barn
URL:https://www.cedarslife.org/events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/looklistenbird", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/look-listen-and-bird/18226708/2026-03-15T10"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/looklistenbird"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Look\, Listen and Bird!
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260315T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260315T113000
UID:260226V3SpfdyEfEKnW3vcCH_MRQ
DESCRIPTION:We will focus (pun intended) on learning stories and 
 field characteristics of local and migrating birds in the variety
  of Sugarloaf habitats\, with an emphasis on ear birding. We’l
 l discuss identification\, migration\, adaptations and our importan
 t role in improving habitat for birds. Let’s try to observe a
 t least 20 species!\n\nMeet at the White Barn parking lot. Ticke
 ts are $10 for general admission\, $5 for youth (12-17 year old
 s\; all minors must be accompanied by a parent or legal guardia
 n)\, students\, Sugarloaf members\, Sugarloaf or RFO volunteers\, 
 and free for children under 12. Wear layers\, appropriate footwea
 r for muddy and/or slippery trails\, bring at least a quart of
  water\, sun protection\, and if desired\, a snack. Binoculars a
 re optional but welcome. Rain cancels. Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/looklistenbird
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.forkinthepath.org/schedule/mushroom-foraging-sonoma-2025-lc6g9-shkzj-99aa8", "Press Democrat": "https://www.forkinthepath.org/schedule/mushroom-foraging-sonoma-2025-lc6g9-shkzj-99aa8"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.forkinthepath.org/schedule/mushroom-foraging-sonoma-2025-lc6g9-shkzj-99aa8"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Sonoma Mushroom Foraging
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260315T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260315T140000
UID:260226AqK7iR7cPUq73O7QnNVoUw
DESCRIPTION:These guided mushroom walks are about 2.5 hours north of San F
 rancisco in Sonoma.  All details you need\, including packing list\, meet
 -up location\, and more will be sent once your booking is confirmed.  Thi
 s is a wonderful weekend adventure to do alone or with friends and family.
  \n\nWhat You'll Learn\n\nThis experiential\, hands-on half-day program i
 s all about the fascinating world of fungi and begins at 10:00 am. Learni
 ng to forage for mushrooms is an ongoing life path. This program will teac
 h you foundational skills to be able to go out foraging on your own. We w
 ill cover mushroom anatomy for identification\, symbiotic tree and plant r
 elationships\, poisonous and edible mushrooms\, and forest safety.  This 
 winter\, it will be possible to find edibles such as porcini\, chanterelle
 \, yellowfoot\, black trumpet\, hedgehog\, and more.  The program also in
 cludes community building\, mindful movement\, a cooking demo\, and a tast
 ing at the end.
LOCATION:Sonoma Coast
URL:https://www.forkinthepath.org/schedule/mushroom-foraging-sonoma-2025-l
 c6g9-shkzj-99aa8
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/the-power-of-letting-go-cultivating-well-being-joy-and-freedom-jb1d26/?lang=en", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/the-power-of-letting-go-cultivating-well-being-joy-and-freedom/18115197/2026-03-15T10"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/the-power-of-letting-go-cultivating-well-being-joy-and-freedom-jb1d26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Power of Letting Go: Cultivating Well-Being\, Joy\, and Freedo
 m
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260315T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260315T150000
UID:260214ypvC_79so0-0AvqyG6lycQ
DESCRIPTION:with James Baraz\, MA\n\nSpring is a natural time to reflect o
 n what we are holding on to and what may be ready to be released. Just wha
 t does the phrase “let go” mean? Renunciation (*nekkhama* in Pāli)\,
  one of the ten perfections\, is often misunderstood as sacrifice—someth
 ing we should do because it’s “good for us.” In early Buddhist teach
 ings\, *nekkhama* is described not as deprivation\, but as a letting go 
 that supports genuine contentment and well-being\, rooted in seeing more c
 learly what leads to suffering and what leads to freedom.\n\nDuring this d
 aylong program\, which includes periods of guided silent sitting and walki
 ng meditation\, participants will explore how habitual grasping—to thoug
 hts\, personal stories\, possessions\, roles\, and a sense of control—sh
 apes inner experience and contributes to stress. Drawing from contemplativ
 e teachings and incorporating perspectives from psychology on attachment a
 nd habitual mental patterns\, our reflections and practices will focus on 
 meeting these patterns with awareness and kindness\, loosening unhelpful s
 elf-stories\, softening the impulse to control\, and cultivating generosit
 y. This program is educational in nature and welcomes both new and experie
 nced practitioners.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/the-power-of-letting-g
 o-cultivating-well-being-joy-and-freedom-jb1d26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.sebastopolgallery.com"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Journey: A Painter's Narrative
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260315T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260315T170000
UID:260128sQd_6ToXX0yv1uKceYDt2w
DESCRIPTION:New Woman and Fox paintings by Teri Sloat celebrate the person
 al journeys we take as we travel outward through landscape trails or inwar
 d through thoughts and dreams. Her ongoing series\, Woman and Fox\, A Jour
 ney\, present rich\, metaphorical paintings that invite you to pause on yo
 ur own path and enjoy the distance you have come.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:https://www.sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/bonsai-and-blossoms/", "Press Democrat": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/bonsai-and-blossoms/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/bonsai-and-blossoms/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Bonsai Show: Bonsai & Blossoms
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260315T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260315T170000
UID:260108zRvLOzhJAEOOQiPj9GUM0A
DESCRIPTION:January 9–March 22\, 2026\n\nStep into a wonderland of bloom
 ing miniature trees to marvel at the living art of bonsai and the season
 ’s first flowers. Then stroll through our Asian Woodland to admire maje
 stic magnolias\, cherries\, and camellias in bloom\, or join a tour or pro
 gram to explore this timeless craft.\n\nThis year’s all-new presentation
  by the skilled artisans of the Redwood Empire Bonsai Society \\(REBS\\) h
 ighlights the grace and vitality of flowering bonsai—trees and shrubs tr
 ained to bloom in exquisite proportion to their diminutive scale. Delicate
  plum\, azalea\, camellia\, cherry\, and apricot bonsai take center stag
 e\, their blossoms appearing just as winter begins to yield to spring. The
 se early bloomers symbolize hope and renewal—reminding us that beauty an
 d resilience can emerge even in the coldest months.\n\nThe exhibition also
  draws inspiration from hanami\, the centuries-old Japanese tradition of 
 celebrating the fleeting beauty of blossoms. The Garden invites visitors t
 o participate in this art of flower appreciation through Hanami Strolls
 —guided walks through the Garden’s Asian woodland where early-blooming
  magnolias\, cherries\, and camellias offer their own ephemeral display.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/bonsai-and-blossoms/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
