BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayletterpressarts.org/for-sale/2026-pochoir", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/introduction-to-pochoir-workshop/18131340/2026-03-21T10"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayletterpressarts.org/for-sale/2026-pochoir"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Introduction to Pochoir Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T160000
UID:260216TdIDwfpXH0S2ZXczz-hMEA
DESCRIPTION:**Pochoir**\, the French term for stencil\, is a well respecte
 d tradition in book arts. Popular during the late 19th and early 20th cent
 uries\, this art-making technique was an advanced form of stencil printing
 . Artists would apply color pigments to paper by hand as an elegant and af
 fordable way to reproduce artwork in color. Join guest artist\, Bettina Pa
 uly in this exciting one-day introduction to pochoir workshop!\n\nBettina 
 will offer a short history lesson\, and share pochoir samples\, including 
 an artist demonstration on how to use pigments with different applicators.
  Students will be encouraged to learn the basics of stencil creation and w
 ill work on images made up of simple shapes to practice their technique. T
 hroughout the day\, an assortment of materials will be on hand to create s
 tencils\; different brushes and their effects will be examined\; and vario
 us ‘dry pigments’ and papers will be investigated as students expand t
 heir pochoir skills. The instructor will also lead a discussion on how stu
 dents can creatively incorporate pochoir into their own artwork\, includin
 g books\, prints\, cards\, and more!\n\nStudents will work on a set of not
 e cards to take home and learn how to make a simple folder for the samples
  that were made during class. The materials fee will include brushes\, ste
 ncils\, paper pigments and an assortment of paper cardstock.\n\n**Please n
 ote:** This class requires some hand dexterity to maneuver an exacto blade
  cutting knife.
LOCATION:North Bay Letterpress Arts
URL:https://www.northbayletterpressarts.org/for-sale/2026-pochoir
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/beaded-ring-workshop/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Beaded Ring Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T130000
UID:260216IYFCCARJhkmhI7nfsKIypA
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday\, March 21\, 2026 10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\
 nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nFiber Arts\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n13\\+\n\nChi
 ldren under the age of 18 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\n$93 – Regi
 stration Cost $7 – Materials Fee $100 – Total Registration CostDiscove
 r the ancient peyote stitch in a fun\, hands-on class and create a bold ri
 ng while learning the basics of bead weaving.\n\nWhat you’ll do\n\nJoin 
 us for a playful dive into an ancient craft. The peyote stitch has been us
 ed for thousands of years across many cultures. In this fun class you’ll
  create a bold beautiful ring using the Even Count Flat Peyote stitch. We
 ’ll cover everything you need to confidently start your own bead weaving
  journey. All materials \\(thread\, needles\, beads\\) will be provided fo
 r the workshop. If students would like to buy needles and thread to take h
 ome they can purchase them directly from the instructor after the workshop
  for a minimal fee. Resources for beading supplies will also be provided. 
 Finger dexterity and good close-up vision are needed for this workshop. Br
 ing your best reading glasses!\n\nMembership has its benefits\n\nAll Silve
 r Memberships and above receive 10% off the registration cost for any clas
 s purchase over $40. Materials fees are not discounted.\n\nBecome a member
  today and find community\, connection\, and creativity.\n\nLocation\n\nRo
 om 201\, Fiber Arts Studio
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/beaded-ring-workshop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/reclaiming-who-we-are-with-self-compassion-kn1m26/?lang=en", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/reclaiming-who-we-are-with-self-compassion/18115202/2026-03-21T10"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/reclaiming-who-we-are-with-self-compassion-kn1m26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Reclaiming Who We Are with Self-Compassion
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T163000
UID:260214KJIrNlr3ZkWWHblFZSyvlQ
DESCRIPTION:with Kristin Neff\, PhD and Caverly Morgan\n\nSelf-compassion 
 helps us let go of identification with the belief that we’re not good en
 ough. With its warm support\, we learn to untangle from our negative thoug
 hts and emotions and embrace our inherent wholeness.\n\nOur unconscious co
 nditioning—influenced by our family\, genetics\, and culture—often tel
 ls us we’re inadequate and need to be different in order to be happy. Co
 mpassion helps us remember who we truly are versus who we’ve been condit
 ioned to be. It transforms our contracted and limited view of ourselves\, 
 opening to a larger\, more connected\, and powerful sense of loving presen
 ce.\n\nResearch shows that self-compassion is strongly linked to psycholog
 ical and physical health\, but our conditioning works against being kind t
 o ourselves. In this program\, researcher Kristin Neff teams up with medit
 ation teacher Caverly Morgan to explore self-compassion from a scientific 
 and contemplative lens\, so that we can respond to difficult moments with 
 greater warmth and perspective.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/reclaiming-who-we-are-
 with-self-compassion-kn1m26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
