X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/ew6dc3w3s87emgn"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Morning Yoga
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260325T083000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260325T094000
UID:260302E0Isyp_AuEimFvSBLmtipA
DESCRIPTION:Regenerative Ayurvedic Yoga with Tirza Dawn Come\, step onto y
 our mat with an open heart and an open mind. Invest in your self care and 
 join us for morning yoga in the OCA studio. $20 per class\, $15 for OCA me
 mbers. Each Wednesday from 9:00-10:15 AM in our Studio. Pay at the door fo
 r a-la-carte sessions or use the links below to pay ahead for four weeks a
 t a time.  Pay Online 4 sessions - OCA members  Pay Online 4 sessions - no
 n members Tirza Dawn Naramore is a yogi\, mother\, artist\, ceremonialist 
 and lover of life. She has been practicing and teaching yoga and meditatio
 n for 30 years and offers yoga retreats and trainings that center on optim
 um health\, self realization and self love. Her teachers are from many yog
 a and tantric traditions\, but her primary lineages are Iyengar and Kali R
 ay.  Tirza is deeply devoted to community building and is honored to have 
 created a number of community supported non profits including Mystic Famil
 y Circus and The AWAKEN Project\, which serves families with children on t
 he autism spectrum. Tirza is proud to be the mother of 3 wild teenagers\, 
 including her incredible son who is diagnosed with autism. Tirza's spiritu
 ality is one of many influences and teachings. Beginning with a Christian 
 up-bringing and being raised on a Christian commune in her early childhood
 \, she later expanded into more earth-based ways. While in her 20's Tirza 
 was adopted into the Native American Church\, where she learned from her r
 elatives a way of living the "Beauty Way." During the 1990's and early 200
 0's\, Tirza lived in San Francisco\, Oakland and Berkeley\, directing the 
 Mystic Family Circus\, which was a performance group dedicated to cultural
  awareness and bridge building. She worked with Cirque du Soleil\, Burning
  Man\, Reclaiming\, Contraband\, CELLspace and other Bay Area art collecti
 ves and non profits to provide conscious entertainment and "prayerformance
 s" for the betterment of humankind and the planet. In 2012\, Tirza helped 
 to found the Buckeye Gathering\, an ancestral skills gathering in Northern
  California which draws teachers and students of all ages to learn ancestr
 al ways of tending the earth and survival skills. Tirza Dawn was the found
 er of yoga programming and the Ayurvedic Yoga Teacher Trainings at the dhy
 ana Center of Ayurveda in Sebastopol\, California\, which operated a commu
 nity center of healing and education from 2010 to 2020.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/ew6dc3w3s87
 emgn
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.cedarslife.org/events"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:"You're My Neighbor" Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260325T090000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260325T180000
UID:260227WbhibpCcGUa2-vtw3r7tmQ
DESCRIPTION:Come out to Point Reyes and celebrate neighbors!   \n\nFrom 
 mooing cows and soaring birds to friendly faces down the road\, Cedars art
 ists take a joyful look at their Marin County neighborhood. This exhibitio
 n explores all the things that make their corner of the world special—op
 en fields\, wild creatures\, familiar people\, and the everyday moments in
  between. Through colorful\, thoughtful\, and imaginative works\, “You
 ’re My Neighbor” celebrates the beauty of living side by side and shar
 ing a place we call home.\n\n​Cedars “You’re My Neighbor!” art exh
 ibition runs from March 3 through April 12\, 2026
LOCATION:Toby's Feed Barn
URL:https://www.cedarslife.org/events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:What About Age? Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260325T090000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260325T180000
UID:260129aQItE4YoYUmUGcMKfBG9Kw
DESCRIPTION:*What About Age?* art exhibit has arrived in Marin County! Or
 iginally displayed at NYU’s Kimmel Windows\, this exhibit explores ageis
 m through contemporary art\, featuring works by both local youth and senio
 r artists.\n\n*What About Age?* is an art exhibit and educational initiat
 ive designed to challenge stereotypes about aging\, address ageism and soc
 ial isolation\, and promote intergenerational dialogue through the lens of
  art.\n\nIn partnership with Youth in Arts\, the exhibit features artworks
  by local youth and senior artists\, showcasing how age intersects with cr
 eativity\, identity\, and experience. Under the guidance of Youth in Arts\
 , these emerging and established artists work side by side to create colla
 borative pieces\, fostering meaningful connections between generations and
  reflecting the exhibit’s core message: art is ageless.\n\nThe exhibit a
 lso includes artwork panels by New York-based writer and illustrator Aubre
 y Hirsch\, first displayed at NYU’s Kimmel Windows and originally organi
 zed by Stacey Gordon\, NYU’s Program Director of Next Phase Adult Caregi
 ving and Retirement at Work Life.\n\nThe new exhibition will be on view at
  the Marin County Civic Center galleries from January 26 to May 6\, 2026. 
 Works will be displayed on the first and third floor exhibits\, Monday to 
 Friday from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m.\n\nThe *What About Age?* art exhibit is prese
 nted by Marin Cultural Association in partnership with Marin Community Fou
 ndation and Youth in Arts. Beyond the art exhibit\, the *What About Age?* 
 initiative offers programming\, led by Vivalon\, designed to challenge age
 ism and provide resources for Marin County's growing aging population.
LOCATION:Marin County Civic Center
URL:https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
