BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Santa Rosa Junior College": "https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/14535-meet-the-author-emilly-prado-funeral-for-flaca"}
X-SOURCE-ID:srjc
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260325T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260325T130000
LOCATION:Ellis Auditorium - Petaluma Campus
SUMMARY:Meet the Author: Emilly Prado\, "Funeral For Flaca"
DESCRIPTION:Emilly Prado is an award-winning writer\, multidisciplinary a
 rtist\, and speaker whose work examines identity\, the systems that shape
  our lives\, and the power of storytelling across mediums. The author wil
 l share the evolving nature of finding her path as a writer\, drawing upo
 n her experiences as a first-generation Chicana and college student\, and
  self-proclaimed troublemaker who struggled with school and mental health
 . Attendees will hear a reading from Funeral for Flaca and view archival 
 childhood photographs to better understand the author and how she found s
 trength through music and writing. Followed by a Q&amp\;A session.  For m
 ore information\, visit: https://events.santarosa.edu/womxns-history-mont
 h-2026 (https://events.santarosa.edu/womxns-history-month-2026)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Emilly Prado is an award-winning writer
 \, multidisciplinary artist\, and speaker whose work examines identity\, 
 the systems that shape our lives\, and the power of storytelling across m
 ediums. The author will share the evolving nature of finding her path as 
 a writer\, drawing upon her experiences as a first-generation Chicana and
  college student\, and self-proclaimed troublemaker who struggled with sc
 hool and mental health. Attendees will hear a reading from Funeral for Fl
 aca and view archival childhood photographs to better understand the auth
 or and how she found strength through music and writing. Followed by a Q&
 amp\;A session.</p><p>  For more information\, visit: <a href="https://ev
 ents.santarosa.edu/womxns-history-month-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopen
 er">https://events.santarosa.edu/womxns-history-month-2026</a></p>
UID:20260325T190000Z-14535@calendar.santarosa.edu
DTSTAMP:20260205T163502Z
