DTSTAMP:20260302T183318
CREATED:20191105T150049Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260302T181555Z
UID:70957-1775928600-1775937600@lutherburbankcenter.org
SUMMARY:Annual Art of Dessert 2026
DESCRIPTION:Back to All Shows\n\n\n\nThe 23rd Annual Art of Dessert\nThe Art of Dessert is LBC’s biggest fundraising event of the year. Over the years\, it has raised more than $8 million to help provide enrichment in the arts to over 1 million children\, families\, and educators. \nMuch anticipated\, spirited\, and delicious\, The Art of Dessert features sumptuous family-style dining\, exceptional Rodney Strong Wine Estates wines\, engaging entertainment\, a silent and live auction\, and\, of course\, decadent desserts by the best bakers in the county! Bid on unique live auction items and enjoy lively entertainment and engaging speakers. Sonoma County’s best fundraiser is a night to remember\, and your support will make a difference for over 50\,000 students\, teachers\, and families in the coming year. \nWHY YOUR SUPPORT MATTERS \nThanks to your support\, Luther Burbank Center for the Arts is the North Bay’s premier arts nonprofit\, a vibrant gathering place providing world-class performances\, a wide variety of community events\, and nationally-recognized education programs that annually serve over 50\,000 students\, teachers\, and families. \nTickets and more information coming soon! \n\n\nWhy Your Support Matters\nThanks to your support\, Luther Burbank Center for the Arts is the North Bay’s premier arts nonprofit\, a vibrant gathering place providing world-class performances\, a wide variety of community events\, and nationally-recognized education programs that annually serve over 50\,000 students\, teachers\, and families. \nTickets and more information coming soon! \n\n\nJoin the Fun – Join the Cause!\nThere are many ways to get involved with The Art of Dessert and support children\, teachers\, families\, and artists in our community\, even from home! \n\n\nApril 4 – 13\, 2026 \nOnline Auction \nBid on amazing wine\, baskets\, gifts\, and experiences in the online silent auction.  \nIf you have an item or experience that you’d like to donate\, please contact Barbara Arriaga\, Member and Donor Relations\, at 707.800.7541 or barriaga@lutherburbankcenter.org \n\n\nSponsorships \nSponsorships are available for this beloved annual event. Get your name in front of hundreds of the most generous and connected members of the community. \nFor more information\, contact Ben Taylor\, Director of Philanthropy\, at 707.800.7505 or btaylor@lutherburbankcenter.org \n\n\n\nWe gratefully acknowledge the LBC Naming Sponsor\, Lytton Rancheria\,\n and Wine Sponsor\, Rodney Strong Wine Estates. \n\n\nThank you to our generous Art of Dessert 2026 sponsors! \n\n Date: April 11\, 2026 \nTime: 5:30pm \nCost: $350 per seat \nLimited number of tickets are available.\nReserve yours by Monday\, March 3 \nCocktail Attire \nLuther Burbank Center for the Arts\nLytton Rancheria Grand Lobby\n50 Mark West Springs Road Santa Rosa \n\n\nBuy Your Tickets\n\nOnline Silent Auction - Coming Soon\n\nPeer to Peer Fundraising Team\n\nDonate to the Event\n\nDirections to LBC
URL:https://lutherburbankcenter.org/event/aod26/
CATEGORIES:2025 - 2026 Season,Special Presentation
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://lutherburbankcenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/AOD-Invitation-Creme-Center-Copy-2.png
END:VEVENT
